Q: How to add a @tailwind CSS rule to CSS checker A: <p>After many tests:</p>
<p>The PostCSS and STYLUS syntax highlighter remove warnings, but CSS Intellisence is incomplete. It does not show the first-utilities classes Tailwind.</p>
<p>I installed '<strong>language-stylus</strong>' plugin, in Visual Studio Code.</p>
<p>Settings&gt; User setting:</p>
<pre><code>&quot;files.associations&quot;: {
   &quot;* .css&quot;: &quot;stylus&quot;
 },
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/burPr.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer">CSS Intellisence is incomplete</a></p>

Q: Blazor Server re-renders component 3x A: <p>Your child component isn't actually re-rendering the UI 3 times. The <code>OnParametersSetAsync</code> <em>is</em> firing 3 times.</p>
<p>Blazor automatically calls <code>StateHasChanged()</code> on the parent after <em>every single event callback finishes-</em> <code>&lt;InputText&gt;</code>: <code>@onfocus</code>, <code>@onblur</code> and <code>@onkeyup</code></p>
<p>And <code>ShouldRender()</code> only controls the HTML DOM diffing and it executes <em>after</em> <code>OnParametersSetAsync</code>. It cannot stop running <code>OnParametersSetAsync</code></p>
<p>Change the parent-</p>
<pre><code>private async Task OnSearchChangedAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e)
{
    if (e?.Code != &quot;Enter&quot; &amp;&amp; e?.Code != &quot;NumpadEnter&quot;) return;
    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_inputText)) return;

    if (_searchText == _inputText) return;

    _searchText = _inputText;

    if (_searchText != _currentArticle)
    {
        _currentArticle = _searchText;
        naviManager.NavigateTo($&quot;/article/{Uri.EscapeDataString(_searchText)}&quot;);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Update child component so that it ignores parent re-renders unless <code>ArticleId</code> actually changed</p>
<pre><code>private bool _shouldRender = true;

protected override bool ShouldRender() =&gt; _shouldRender;

protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
{
    if (ArticleId == _lastSearchText)
    {
        _shouldRender = false;
        return;
    }

    _shouldRender = true;
    _lastSearchText = ArticleId;

    await GetArticlePics();
}
</code></pre>
